  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "A temple vault in Kerala has stayed shut since the 1880s. Six chambers sit under Thiruvananthapuram's Padmanabhaswamy temple, labelled simply A to F.",
        "visual_query": "south indian temple gopuram kerala",
        "visual_fallback": "indian temple"
      },
      {
        "narration": "In 2011 India's Supreme Court ordered five of them opened and inventoried. Vault A alone gave up over a hundred thousand objects.",
        "visual_query": "kerala temple stone corridor pillars",
        "visual_fallback": "stone corridor"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Eight hundred kilos of gold coins, some of them struck around 200 BCE. And the sixth door simply stayed closed.",
        "visual_query": "gold coins treasure hoard closeup",
        "visual_fallback": "gold coins"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Not for want of a crowbar. A temple ritual in 2011 declared Vault B a forbidden zone, and the priests have opposed opening it ever since.",
        "visual_query": "indian temple oil lamps ritual",
        "visual_fallback": "oil lamps"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The court sided with custom. In July 2020 it handed control back to the former Travancore royal family, and Vault B is still sealed today.",
        "visual_query": "thiruvananthapuram kerala city temple aerial",
        "visual_fallback": "kerala cityscape"
      }
    ],
